#: ../../../install_windows.md:1
msgid ""
"<div class=\"warning\">\n"
"WARNING: Current Windows support is experimental.\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:5
msgid "Binary Installation on Windows 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:7
msgid ""
"Only the following Ignition packages are currently available on `conda-"
"forge`, the package manager Ignition uses for Windows binary installations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:9
msgid "`ign-cmake`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:10
msgid "`ign-common`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:11
msgid "`ign-fuel-tools`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:12
msgid "`ign-math`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:13
msgid "`ign-msgs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:14
msgid "`ign-physics`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:15
msgid "`ign-plugin`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:16
msgid "`ign-rendering`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:17
msgid "`ign-tools`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:18
msgid "`ign-transport`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:20
msgid ""
"The above mentioned Ignition packages are available in Windows 10 using the "
"[conda-forge package manager](https://conda-forge.org/), and the Ignition "
"feedstock recipes can be found [here](https://github.com/conda-forge?"
"q=libignition&type=&language=)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:23
msgid ""
"The remaining packages currently have an [outstanding ticket](https://github."
"com/conda-forge/staged-recipes/issues/13551), and will not be supported "
"until they are added to the `conda-forge` feedstock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:26
msgid ""
"Additionally, command line tools, the DART physics engine, and some tests "
"are not currently supported in Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:28
msgid "In order to use `conda-forge`, you will need to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:29
msgid ""
"Install a [Conda package management system](https://docs.conda.io/projects/"
"conda/en/latest/user-guide/install/download.html). Miniconda suffices. You "
"will likely want to check the box to add `conda` to your `PATH` during the "
"installation process so that you won't have to do this step manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:33
msgid ""
"Open a Windows command prompt, being sure to have `conda` added to your "
"Windows `PATH` system environment variable (you may also need to open a new "
"command prompt to see any `PATH` changes reflected)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:37
msgid ""
"If you did not add Conda to your `PATH` environment variable   during Conda "
"installation, you may need to navigate to the   location of `condabin` in "
"order to use the `conda` command.   To find `condabin`, search for "
"\"Anaconda Prompt\" in the   Windows search field near the Windows button, "
"open it, run   `where conda`, and look for a line containing the directory "
"`condabin`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:44
msgid "Create and activate a new Conda environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:45
msgid ""
"conda create -n ign-ws\n"
"conda activate ign-ws\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:49
msgid ""
"Install desired Ignition packages, since all of Ignition isn't currently "
"supported, you will need to choose which package(s) you want to install "
"based on your application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:51
msgid "conda install libignition-<package_name><#> --channel conda-forge\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:54
msgid ""
"Be sure to replace `<package_name>` with your desired package name (ie, "
"common, msgs, etc.)   and `<#>` with the release version.  If left "
"unspecified, `conda-forge` will install the   most recently stable release "
"packages.  Be sure to check the   [high level install instructions](install) "
"for corresponding version numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:59
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:61
msgid "You can view all available versions of a specific package with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:62
msgid "conda search libignition-<package_name>* --channel conda-forge\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:65
msgid "and view their dependencies with"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:66
msgid "conda search libignition-<package_name>* --channel conda-forge --info\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:69
msgid "and install a specific minor version with"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:70
msgid ""
"conda install libignition-<package_name>=<major>.<minor>.<patch> --channel "
"conda-forge\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:73
msgid ""
"where `<major>` is the major release number, `<minor>` is the minor release "
"number, and `<patch` is the patch release number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:75
msgid "Uninstalling binary install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:77
msgid ""
"If you need to uninstall Ignition or switch to a source-based install once "
"you have already installed the library from binaries, run the following "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:80
msgid "conda uninstall libignition-<package_name> --channel conda-forge\n"
msgstr ""

